<node id="Amyloid Cascade Hypothesis">
  <data key="d0">mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">The accumulation of amyloid-beta (Aβ) peptides in the brain, primarily Aβ42, forms oligomers and plaques. This is considered a primary initiating event in Alzheimer's disease pathogenesis, leading to synaptic dysfunction, tau pathology, and neurodegeneration. Biomarkers like CSF Aβ42 levels and amyloid PET tracers (PIB, AV45, FBB) reflect this accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d2">66</data>
</node>
